From a4c23312845af03f6de1c18089243d2e4a054568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:48:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] shared: the no-follow store writer, private key folders,
 Wallguard and Encrypted DNS defaults

reaper_store_io.h is the one writer for the long-term store: every level is
opened from its trusted parent with O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY, files O_NOFOLLOW +
S_ISREG, a replace goes through an O_EXCL temp and rename, and appends rotate
at a cap. A USB store is a volume other people can write (guest shares map to
uid 0), so a root write by path could be steered by a planted link; rstore and
the C writers use this instead. reaper_store.h gains the shell reader of the
watchdog's published store location and the Wallguard / Dreadwatch / Encrypted
DNS row tokens. reaper_tmpsafe: /tmp/wallguard, /tmp/rednsd and /tmp/reaper_nx
as root 0755 with a nobody-owned 0700 run/ (reaper_secure_dir_for), and
reaper_write_changed() so an unchanged config file is not rewritten.
reaper_jfile.c: reaper_private_dir() for a folder only root may enter (the
IPsec CA and key folders). defaults.c: wallguard_enable, wallguard_mode,
reaper_dot_srv, reaper_doh_block - every new feature off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
